A semicircle has symmetry, so the center is exactly at the midpoint of the 2 side on the rectangle, making the radius, by the Pythagorean Theorem, <math>\sqrt{1^2+1^2}=\sqrt{2}</math>. The area is <math>\frac{2\pi}{2}=\boxed{\textbf{(C)}\ \pi}</math>.

==List of steps==
1. Draw a picture, realize the radius comes from the midpoint of rectangle
2. Using the pythagorean theorm, solve for the radius with is square root of 2
3. Solve for the area of the circle using the radius pi times radius squared, with will give you 2pi
4. Divide by 2, getting pi
